## Quality and lineage

- Record source identity, acquisition, transformations, joins, filters, and output lineage.
- Define required fields, null behavior, uniqueness, ordering, time semantics, and validation only where applicable.
- Keep migrations and compatibility boundaries traceable.
- Distinguish raw, derived, current, historical, and test data.
- Record access, retention, privacy, backup, and recovery rules supported by evidence.

